<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block">
  <!--
    map-filter-fold.mml
    Restricted Content MathML contract for typed collection transforms.

    This collection fold is distinct from the six-phase K'UHUL fold. The
    operators are declarative here; runtime lowering and XCFE admission are
    required before any execution.
  -->

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Pipeline</mi><mo>=</mo>
      <mi>Fold</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>oplus</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>seed</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>Filter</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>Map</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:functional:v1">fold</csymbol>
        <ci>oplus</ci><ci>seed</ci>
        <apply>
          <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:functional:v1">filter</csymbol>
          <ci>P</ci>
          <apply><csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:functional:v1">map</csymbol><ci>f</ci><ci>X</ci></apply>
        </apply>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
For input collection X, map applies pure transform f to each element, filter
retains elements satisfying predicate P, and fold accumulates the resulting
ordered sequence using seed and binary step oplus. Types and traversal order
must be declared by the consuming program contract.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Map</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>=</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>i</mn></msub><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>]</mo><msub><mrow/><mi>i</mi></msub>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply><csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:functional:v1">map</csymbol><ci>f</ci><ci>X</ci></apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Map preserves input cardinality and item order. In KHANARY it may project
typed gram or graph candidates into vector/metric records. A transform must
declare its input and output types and effects.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Filter</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>=</mo><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub>
      <mo>|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&#x2208;</mo><mi>X</mi>
      <mo>&#x2227;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply><csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:functional:v1">filter</csymbol><ci>P</ci><ci>X</ci></apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Filter is stable: retained elements preserve their input order. It can remove
invalid bindings or candidates that fail a declared predicate. A filter may
consume an XCFE admission result, but cannot replace or mint XCFE authority.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Fold</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#x2295;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a0</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub>
      <mspace width="1em"/><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub>
      <mo>=</mo><mi>&#x2295;</mi><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub>
      <mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply><csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:functional:v1">fold</csymbol>
        <ci>oplus</ci><ci>a0</ci><ci>X</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Fold reduces an ordered collection from an explicit initial accumulator.
Associativity, identity, parallelization, and empty-input behavior must be
declared by the selected step contract; the runtime must not assume them.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>TypedExecution</mi><mo>=</mo>
      <mi>ParseMathML</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>LowerToKAST</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mi>CheckTypesAndEffects</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>XCFEAdmission</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mi>ExecuteInPhase</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply><csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:functional:v1">ExecutionBoundary</csymbol>
        <list><ci>ParseMathML</ci><ci>LowerToKAST</ci><ci>CheckTypesAndEffects</ci>
          <ci>XCFEAdmission</ci><ci>ExecuteInPhase</ci></list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Content MathML is a machine-readable expression surface, not an execution
engine. Lowering must preserve types and effects. XCFE and host authorization
remain authoritative. Functional Fold reduces a collection; K'UHUL fold
denotes the Pop, Wo, Yax, Sek, Ch'en, Xul lifecycle.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <annotation encoding="text/plain">
MapFilterFold contract invariants:
1. Map transforms typed values and is pure unless an explicit effect contract says otherwise.
2. Filter preserves input order and cannot substitute for XCFE admission.
3. Fold requires an explicit initial accumulator, step, and traversal order.
4. No algebraic or parallel-execution properties are assumed without declaration.
5. Parsing MathML does not itself grant execution or persistent-write authority.
  </annotation>
</math>
